#pragma code_page(65001)
// res/lang/ml.rc -- Malayalam (Malayalam script), the strings of the interface for `[general] language = "ml"`.
//
// Stage E108, group A: the two string tables of this language -- the dialog block and the menu
// block -- in the order of en.rc. An adaptation, not a letter-for-letter translation (owner's word
// 198.14); the glossary of the language is l10n/glossary/ml.tsv in the control contour. Keys stay
// in Latin letters as the hotkey field prints them (RULES 4); the quotation marks are “ ” and the
// full stop of a sentence is the ordinary «.» (RULES 3). The reader is addressed in the verbal noun
// imperative («-ുക») as Windows does in Malayalam, which has no gender of the reader; the verbs of
// the first person carry no gender either, so the voice of the author needs no choice (RULES 14).
// No zero-width joiners: the words are written so that they stand without U+200C / U+200D.
//
// ⚠ In an .rc string a backslash is an escape -- one backslash is written as two -- and a double
// quote inside a string is written as two double quotes. The code page line above is this
// file's own: without it rc.exe reads the file in the ANSI code page, silently.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Malayalam — `[general] language = "ml"`.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
